<title>THAILAND: Thai Danu opens at 36 baht on resumption.</title>
<headline>Thai Danu opens at 36 baht on resumption.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Danu Bank Plc opened at 36 baht on resumption of trading on Tuesday after the company scrapped its merger plan with Finance One Plc on Friday.</p>
<p>Thai Danu was earlier suspended by the bourse since February 28 when it was last traded at 46 baht.  </p>
<p>Thai Danu Bank, ranked 11th among 15 Thai banks, rose to its intraday high of 41 baht nine minutes after the market opened. It was at 39.50 baht at 0343 GMT.</p>
<p>Analysts said the failed Thai Danu-Finance One merger plan should be good news for the bank.</p>
<p>&quot;The collapse of the merger plan would spare Thai Danu financial burden of absorbing Finance One's weak assets,&quot; said Bunsom Kesapradist of Asia Credit.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
